valid range (admissibility automatic): r >= 9

  r   rank d(mu) (Q)   mod p1   mod p2   dim cone X^*   dim X^*   Hessian route (wk9_s55_ranks2)
   9               7        7        7              7         6                6   agree
  10               7        7        7              7         6                6   agree
  11               7        7        7              7         6                6   agree
  12               7        7        7              7         6                6   agree

  The two routes agree at every r in the valid range.  The Jacobian has
  only 8 columns, so the rank saturates at 7 and dim X^* at 6 = 2n-2 --
  because the Gauss image is a linear projection of the 6-dimensional
  Segre variety of rank-1 4x4 matrices.  That is the geometric reason
  k = 6 cannot be lowered: it is the dual dimension of det_4 itself, and
  once r >= 9 the projection is generically finite so no linear section
  makes it smaller.

  NOTE the Hessian-route column is quoted from results/logs/s55_ranks2.log
  and asserted against, not recomputed here.
